This is a breaking change, could we instead use the factory version of `.Singleton` so we preserve the type DI sees as `RedisCache`?
Pseudo code:
```csharp
services.Add(ServiceDescriptor.Singleton<IDistributedCache, RedisCache>(provider =>
{
    return new RedisCacheImpl(provider.GetRequiredService<IOptions<RedisCacheOptions>>(),
        provider.GetRequiredService<ILogger<RedisCache>>());
}));
```

I just tested this locally, and using `services.Add(ServiceDescriptor.Singleton<IDistributedCache, RedisCache>())` and then doing the below fails:

```csharp
[Fact]
public void AddStackExchangeRedisCache_RegistersRedisCache()
{
    // Arrange
    var services = new ServiceCollection();

    // Act
    services.AddStackExchangeRedisCache(options => { });

    // Assert
    var serviceProvider = services.BuildServiceProvider();
    var redisCache = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<RedisCache>();

    Assert.NotNull(redisCache);
}
```

